# Settings page voice

The settings page is **titles/headers**, controls, and **a few pithy disclaimers**. It is not talking to the developer.

Do not add how-to copy, “default N means…”, em-dash essays, or toast/button tutorials. The control’s own label is the instruction. If it needs a warning, one blunt sentence (same voice as “Naive GPU and Perturbation are early-dev and still buggy”).
